cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyMack in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "pyMack: open-source linear stability theory for compressible and hypersonic boundary-layer transition"
abstract: >-
  pyMack is an open-source Python package for linear stability theory (LST) of
  compressible and hypersonic boundary layers using Chebyshev spectral
  collocation. It computes disturbance growth rates, eigenvalue spectra, neutral
  curves and N-factors, including Mack's second mode. Validated against
  Orszag (1971), Mack (1984), and Özgen & Kırcalı (2008).
type: software
authors:
